## 5. What Does Not Change

- Layer 1 hard constraints — unchanged (50% concentration limit still enforced)
- Signal hierarchy (CR010) — unchanged; Framework E is additive, not a replacement
- Individual stock entry frameworks A, B, C, D — unchanged
- Narrative boundary rule (CR011) — unchanged
- Response format — unchanged
- Hard stop-loss and profit target — unchanged

---

## 6. Success Criteria

| Scenario | Expected Behaviour |
|---|---|
| Cash < 30%, top-3 stocks in portfolio | Framework E not triggered, normal per-stock reasoning |
| Cash > 50%, top-ranked stock down due to macro, thesis intact | Framework E triggered; averaging down recommended with scale guidance |
| Cash > 75%, no Priority 2 negative catalysts on top-3 stocks | Framework E triggered; deployment recommended even if RSI imperfect |
| Cash > 50%, all top-3 stocks have active negative catalysts | Framework E triggered; cash hold explicitly justified with written reasoning |
| Cash > 50%, averaging down would breach 50% concentration limit | Framework E triggered; partial deployment recommended up to concentration limit |
| Cash hold recommended | Explicit opportunity cost stated in response (what return is foregone) |

---

## 7. Out of Scope

- This CR does not change how the portfolio cash balance is tracked or updated
- This CR does not introduce automatic trade execution
- This CR does not override Priority 2 negative catalysts — a stock with an active negative catalyst still blocks entry even under cash drag conditions (except Option B partial deploy, which requires no active Priority 2 catalyst)
- This CR does not change the 50% single-position concentration limit
- This is a prompt architecture change only — no application code changes required